   "bend": "f = lambda_3 - lambda_2^2 / lambda_1 from the pooled marked frequencies of the depth arms (copies pooled after the mirror-pair and heterogeneity gates below), each corrected to the model's readout by the eight readout preparations (decisions.readout), with the binomial variances at the observed frequencies and the readout covariance, delta method over the three arms; z = (f - model.f) / SE; z <= -3 reads 'the retention law bends beyond the model at mirrored positions', which excludes positional drift linear in position as the cause; z >= 3 reads 'bends upward of the model'; otherwise 'no bend beyond the model resolved at mirrored positions'",
   "beside": "rho_4 against the retained fits' continuations in standard errors, the fits that end on a rate bound, and whether the retention decreases with depth; none decides",
   "family": "generalized least squares (the full covariance of the four corrected frequencies) of three nested families to rho_k = lambda_k / model.lambda_k at k = 1 to 4 (gororoba_quantum/grover_depth_families.py): the geometric family a s^k, and the coherent families a s^k R_k(x), R_k(x) the marked probability of the committed depth-k circuit above the uniform floor, relative to its ideal value, by exact simulation with every CZ applying the conditional phase pi + x (cz_phase, |x| <= 0.3 rad) or every PRX rotating by theta (1 + x) (prx_amplitude, |x| <= 0.10); the prefactor a is free in all three and s lies in [0.30, 1.20]. 'neither family fits' when the geometric chi-square exceeds its 0.99 quantile at two degrees of freedom (9.21) and the better coherent one exceeds its quantile at one (6.63); else 'coherent' when the better coherent fit is adequate and the geometric chi-square exceeds its own by delta_resolve; else 'geometric' when the geometric fit is adequate and the model's chi-square (rho = 1) exceeds the geometric one by delta_resolve; else 'unresolved'. delta_resolve is the smallest threshold at which the geometric truth read as coherent, either coherent truth read as geometric and the model read as either family each have probability at most 0.01 (decisions.calibration). A fit on a bound blocks a reading only when the reading rests on it: 'coherent' blocks when the coherent fit sits on a bound, every other reading when either fit does, as 'out of domain'. Gating: a copy below half its planned kept shots leaves its depth together with the copy at its mirrored position, a depth without kept shots is unusable, the bend needs depths 1 to 3 and stands on its own, the family comparison needs all four depths, and a decision whose depths are unusable reads 'not evaluated' without blocking the other",
   "function": "grover_depth_families.read_copies",
